  "content": {
    "id": "p48-q17-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Find the normal to $y=e^x-x$ when $x=\\ln 2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=2-x$.",
      "worked": "The tangent gradient is\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=e^x-1\\\\f'(\\ln 2)&=e^{\\ln 2}-1\\\\f'(\\ln 2)&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe normal gradient is\n$$\\begin{align*}m_N&=-\\frac{1}{1}\\\\m_N&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe point on the curve is found from\n$$\\begin{align*}f(\\ln 2)&=e^{\\ln 2}-\\ln 2\\\\f(\\ln 2)&=2-\\ln 2.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the point-gradient formula at $(\\ln 2,2-\\ln 2)$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y-(2-\\ln 2)&=-(x-\\ln 2)\\\\y-(2-\\ln 2)&=-x+\\ln 2\\\\y&=2-x.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
